# Amanita scout, exploding: a wedge of the cap's rim (3 of 5). One of the fourteen pieces the amanita scout bursts into, each the scout (the
# amanita_scout part, so they follow its edits) intersected with a cell; the cells split all of space with no gap or overlap, so
# the pieces fit together exactly and together are the scout. The cell is in the scout's inner flesh, which shows on the cut faces.
#
# How space is cut: a plane under the gills takes the cap off the stem. The cap is a Voronoi of six seeds (a domed middle and five
# rim wedges). Below it, the amanita_scout_core part holds the stem, bulb and ring clear of the floating eyes and hands: inside it
# the stem breaks under the ring and above the bulb, and the bulb in two; outside it each eye and each hand is a piece of its own,
# whole. Low detail: debris lives a few seconds. The surface is shaded as the whole scout's (its thickness and occlusion measured on
# the scout), so the pieces put together look like the scout itself.
format 1
surface part=amanita_scout

Detail detail=0.5
    Intersection
        Part part=amanita_scout
        Material material=amanita_flesh
            Intersection
                # Above the cut under the gills
                Plane normal=(-0.03, -0.9994, -0.02) height=1.1193
                # Nearer this piece's seed than each other one
                Plane normal=(0.7312, 0.47, -0.4943) height=-0.5098
                Plane normal=(0.9835, 0, -0.1811) height=-0.0107
                Plane normal=(0.8443, 0, 0.5358) height=-0.0637
                Plane normal=(-0.0838, 0, -0.9965) height=-0.054
                Plane normal=(0.6191, 0, -0.7853) height=-0.0159
